IMPORT prelude

-- Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 (Singapore) -- the minimum retirement age and the bar on age dismissal (ss 2, 4, 6), who is
-- eligible for re-employment and what the employer must do (ss 7, 7A, 7C), the remedies and their time limits (ss 8, 8A, 8B, 8C),
-- and the penalties and composition (ss 4(3), 8(7), 8B(13), 9(2), 9A(2), 9B, 9C, 10).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 1/7/2022"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/RRA1993.txt. The latest amendment annotated is Act 38 of 2021, with effect from 1 July 2022.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: it decides when an employee in Singapore can be retired and whether the
-- employer must offer re-employment after that, which every older worker meets. SCOPED to the rules an employee or employer meets
-- directly. Not encoded: the officers (s 3), the effect of continuing to work past the specified age without re-employment
-- (s 7A(2), (3)), reckoning of service (s 7B, s 7C(6)), the E1/E2 transfer mechanics (s 7C(2), (7), (8)), the Minister's and the
-- Tribunal's discretion on amounts (ss 8(3), (4), 8B(6), (10), 8C(3)), investigation powers (s 9(1), 9A(1), (3)), exemptions,
-- tripartite guidelines and regulations (ss 11, 11B, 12). THE ACT DOES NOT STATE THE AGES THEMSELVES: s 4(1) and s 7A(11) only fix
-- the ranges (62 to 65; 67 to 70) within which the Minister specifies them by Gazette notification, and no notification was
-- retrieved. Every age here is therefore a parameter.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 -- retirement and re-employment`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the higher of` MEANS IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `2 -- the specified age and what counts as a dismissal`

-- s 2(1): "specified age", in relation to an employee, means "the higher of" (a) the employee's prescribed minimum retirement age;
-- (b) the retirement age stipulated in the employee's contract of service.
-- s 2(2): an employee is treated as dismissed if (a) the contract is terminated by the employer, "whether it is so terminated by
-- notice or without notice"; or (b) the employer "retires the employee, or requires or causes that employee to retire or resign on
-- the ground of age".
GIVEN `the prescribed minimum retirement age` IS A NUMBER, `the contractual retirement age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the specified age` MEANS `the higher of` `the prescribed minimum retirement age` `the contractual retirement age`

GIVEN `the employer terminated the contract` IS A BOOLEAN, `the employer retired the employee or made the employee retire or resign on the ground of age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee is treated as dismissed` IF
    `the employer terminated the contract` OR `the employer retired the employee or made the employee retire or resign on the ground of age`

§§ `4, 7A(11) -- the permitted ranges for the two ages`

-- s 4(1): the Minister may by Gazette notification specify the prescribed minimum retirement age for any class of employees, "which
-- must be at least 62 years but not more than 65 years".
-- s 7A(11): likewise the prescribed re-employment age, "which must be at least 67 years but not more than 70 years".
GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the minimum retirement age is within the permitted range` IF
    `the age` AT LEAST 62 AND `the age` AT MOST 65

GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the re-employment age is within the permitted range` IF
    `the age` AT LEAST 67 AND `the age` AT MOST 70

§§ `4(2), 4(3), 6 -- no dismissal on the ground of age below the minimum retirement age`

-- s 4(2): "Despite any other written law, contract of service or collective agreement, an employer must not dismiss an employee on
-- the ground of age before that employee attains the employee's prescribed minimum retirement age." (3): an offence, fine up to
-- $5,000 or imprisonment up to 6 months or both.
-- s 6: a term of a contract of service or collective agreement "which provides for a retirement age which is below the employee's
-- prescribed minimum retirement age is void to the extent that it is so less favourable".
-- s 2(3): N years of age is attained "on or after the Nth ... anniversary" of birth -- so ages here are whole completed years.
GIVEN `the employee's age` IS A NUMBER, `the prescribed minimum retirement age` IS A NUMBER, `dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN, `on the ground of age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dismissal contravenes section 4(2)` IF
    `dismissed` AND `on the ground of age` AND `the employee's age` LESS THAN `the prescribed minimum retirement age`

GIVEN `the contractual retirement age` IS A NUMBER, `the prescribed minimum retirement age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contractual retirement term is void` IF
    `the contractual retirement age` LESS THAN `the prescribed minimum retirement age`

§§ `7 -- eligibility for re-employment`

-- s 7(1): eligible if (a) "the employee is born on or after 1 July 1952"; and (b) the employer assesses the employee as (i) having
-- "at least satisfactory work performance"; and (ii) "being medically fit to continue working".
-- s 7(2): the employee "is presumed to be medically fit to continue working, unless the employer of the employee proves, on a balance
-- of probabilities, that the employee is not medically fit".
GIVEN `birth year` IS A NUMBER, `birth month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `born on or after 1 July 1952` IF
    `birth year` GREATER THAN 1952 OR (`birth year` EQUALS 1952 AND `birth month` AT LEAST 7)

GIVEN `birth year` IS A NUMBER, `birth month` IS A NUMBER, `work performance at least satisfactory` IS A BOOLEAN, `employer proved the employee medically unfit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee is eligible for re-employment` IF
        `born on or after 1 July 1952` `birth year` `birth month`
    AND `work performance at least satisfactory`
    AND (NOT `employer proved the employee medically unfit`)

§§ `7A(1), 7C(1), 7C(3) -- the duty to re-employ, and the employment assistance payment`

-- s 7A(1): "Subject to section 7C", an employer must, before an eligible employee attains the specified age, offer re-employment, and
-- the obligation runs "from the time that employee attains the specified age, until that employee attains the employee's prescribed
-- re-employment age".
-- s 7C(1): section 7A does not apply if the employer "is unable to find a vacancy ... that is suitable for the eligible employee,
-- despite making reasonable attempts to do so in accordance with the tripartite guidelines", AND (a) the employer offers an
-- employment assistance payment; or (b) another employer offers to employ the employee in lieu and the employee accepts.
-- s 7C(3): no payment need be offered to an eligible employee who "informs his or her employer of the employee's decision not to
-- continue to be employed" on or after the specified age.
GIVEN `eligible` IS A BOOLEAN, `no suitable vacancy despite reasonable attempts` IS A BOOLEAN, `payment offered` IS A BOOLEAN, `another employer's offer accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer must offer re-employment` IF
        `eligible`
    AND NOT (    `no suitable vacancy despite reasonable attempts`
             AND (`payment offered` OR `another employer's offer accepted`))

GIVEN `eligible` IS A BOOLEAN, `no suitable vacancy despite reasonable attempts` IS A BOOLEAN, `another employer's offer accepted` IS A BOOLEAN, `employee said they will not continue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an employment assistance payment must be offered` IF
        `eligible`
    AND `no suitable vacancy despite reasonable attempts`
    AND (NOT `another employer's offer accepted`)
    AND (NOT `employee said they will not continue`)

GIVEN `the employee's age` IS A NUMBER, `the specified age` IS A NUMBER, `the prescribed re-employment age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the re-employment obligation is running` IF
    `the employee's age` AT LEAST `the specified age` AND `the employee's age` LESS THAN `the prescribed re-employment age`

§§ `7A(6), 7A(7) -- the length of a re-employment contract`

-- s 7A(6): "Unless otherwise agreed by the parties to a re-employment contract, the period of employment stipulated in the contract
-- must not be less than one year at any one time."
-- s 7A(7): where the period from the start of re-employment to the prescribed re-employment age "is less than one year", the contract
-- "may be for that shorter period". (Months are used as the unit.)
GIVEN `months until the re-employment age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum term in months` MEANS `the lower of` 12 `months until the re-employment age`

GIVEN `term in months` IS A NUMBER, `months until the re-employment age` IS A NUMBER, `the parties agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the re-employment term is long enough` IF
    `the parties agreed otherwise` OR `term in months` AT LEAST `the minimum term in months` `months until the re-employment age`

§§ `8, 8A, 8B, 8C -- where a dispute goes and how long the employee has`

-- s 8(1): an employee "below the specified age" who considers he or she has been unlawfully dismissed on the ground of age may,
-- "within one month of the dismissal", make written representations to the Minister to be reinstated.
-- s 8A(4): a re-employment dispute is over (a) denial for failing the s 7(1) criteria; (b) denial for want of a suitable vacancy;
-- (c) the reasonableness of the terms of a re-employment offer; (d) the reasonableness of the employment assistance payment.
-- s 8A(1): for (a) or (b), first notify the Commissioner "no later than one month after the last day of the employee's employment",
-- then representations to the Minister under s 8B.
-- s 8A(2): an employee "who attains the specified age on or after 1 January 2012" who considers he or she was dismissed without just
-- cause or excuse on or after the specified age must likewise notify the Commissioner within one month of the last day.
-- s 8A(3): for (c) or (d), a mediation request to the Commissioner under the Employment Claims Act 2016 "not later than 6 months after
-- the last day", then a claim at the Employment Claims Tribunal (s 8C(1)).
-- s 8B(2): representations to the Minister "no later than one month after the conclusion of any conciliation".
DECLARE Dispute IS ONE OF
    `denied for failing the eligibility criteria`
    `denied for want of a suitable vacancy`
    `the terms of the re-employment offer`
    `the amount of the employment assistance payment`

DECLARE Forum IS ONE OF
    `the Commissioner then the Minister`
    `mediation then the Employment Claims Tribunal`

GIVEN `the dispute` IS A Dispute
GIVETH A Forum
`where the dispute goes` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the dispute`
    WHEN `denied for failing the eligibility criteria` THEN `the Commissioner then the Minister`
    WHEN `denied for want of a suitable vacancy` THEN `the Commissioner then the Minister`
    OTHERWISE `mediation then the Employment Claims Tribunal`

DECLARE Step IS ONE OF
    `representations against an age dismissal`
    `notice of a re-employment dispute to the Commissioner`
    `notice of a dismissal after the specified age to the Commissioner`
    `mediation request over terms or payment`
    `representations to the Minister after conciliation`

GIVEN `the step` IS A Step
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the time limit in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the step`
    WHEN `mediation request over terms or payment` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 1

GIVEN `the step` IS A Step, `months elapsed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the step is in time` IF
    `months elapsed` AT MOST `the time limit in months` `the step`

GIVEN `year the specified age was attained` IS A NUMBER, `dismissed on or after the specified age` IS A BOOLEAN, `considers the dismissal without just cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the just-cause route under sections 8A(2) and 8B is open` IF
        `year the specified age was attained` AT LEAST 2012
    AND `dismissed on or after the specified age`
    AND `considers the dismissal without just cause`

GIVEN `the employee's age` IS A NUMBER, `the specified age` IS A NUMBER, `considers the dismissal on the ground of age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the age-dismissal route under section 8 is open` IF
    `considers the dismissal on the ground of age` AND `the employee's age` LESS THAN `the specified age`

-- s 8B(3), (4) and s 8C(2): for an employee who is dismissed, representations to the Minister under s 8B(1), representations under
-- s 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960, and a Tribunal claim over the payment amount (s 8A(4)(d)) each "operate as a bar" to
-- the other two in respect of that dismissal.
DECLARE Route IS ONE OF
    `section 8B representations`
    `Industrial Relations Act section 35(3) representations`
    `Tribunal claim over the payment amount`

GIVEN `the route` IS A Route
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the route number` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the route`
    WHEN `section 8B representations` THEN 1
    WHEN `Industrial Relations Act section 35(3) representations` THEN 2
    OTHERWISE 3

GIVEN `the employee was dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the route taken first` IS A Route, `the route tried later` IS A Route
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the later route is barred` IF
    `the employee was dismissed` AND NOT ((`the route number` `the route taken first`) EQUALS (`the route number` `the route tried later`))

§§ `4(3), 8(7), 8B(13), 9(2), 9A(2), 9B, 9C, 10 -- penalties and composition`

-- s 4(3) age dismissal, s 9(2) obstructing or lying to an investigating officer, s 9B(1) obstructing an employee appearing before the
-- Commissioner: fine up to $5,000 or 6 months. s 8(7) and s 8B(13) failing to comply with the Minister's direction: $10,000 or
-- 12 months. s 9A(2) (ignoring a summons) and s 9B(2) (obstructing an entry, inquiry or investigation) state no penalty, so s 9C
-- applies: $5,000 or 6 months, "and for a subsequent offence under the same section" $10,000 or 12 months.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `dismissing on the ground of age below the minimum retirement age`
    `failing to comply with a section 8 direction`
    `failing to comply with a section 8B direction`
    `obstructing or lying to an investigating officer`
    `obstructing an employee appearing before the Commissioner`
    `neglecting a summons`
    `obstructing an entry, inquiry or investigation`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the general penalty in section 9C applies` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `neglecting a summons` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `obstructing an entry, inquiry or investigation` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `a subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `the general penalty in section 9C applies` `the offence`
    THEN IF `a subsequent offence` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000
    ELSE CONSIDER `the offence`
         WHEN `failing to comply with a section 8 direction` THEN 10000
         WHEN `failing to comply with a section 8B direction` THEN 10000
         OTHERWISE 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `a subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF (`the maximum fine` `the offence` `a subsequent offence`) EQUALS 10000 THEN 12 ELSE 6

-- s 10(1): an investigating officer, with the Commissioner's approval, may compound a prescribed compoundable offence for "a sum not
-- exceeding the lower of" (a) "one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence"; (b) "$1,000". Which
-- offences are compoundable is left to regulations (s 10(3)), not retrieved.
GIVEN `the maximum fine for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS `the lower of` (`the maximum fine for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 1000
